# What the Python pool's image installs (PLAN.md 4.1, decision 8): only the libraries with no Rust
# equivalent yet, each pinned, and everything they need at the version ace3's virtualenv has, so
# 3.3's comparison with ace3 isn't comparing library versions.
#
# requirements.txt is this file resolved, with a hash for every file. To change a pin, edit this
# file, then run tools/python/lock.
#
# ace3/installer/requirements-pinned.txt. Nothing here calls olevba or rtfobj since PLAN.md 4.10, but
# pcodedmp imports oletools.olevba and oletools.common.codepages, and msoffcrypto needs olefile, so
# oletools stays until 4.12. The module that called msoffcrypto left at 4.11, but
# XLMMacroDeobfuscator imports it at its top and decrypts with it, and tools/library-diff compares with
# it, so it stays until 4.12 too.
oletools==0.60.2
msoffcrypto-tool==6.0.0
pcodedmp==1.2.6
cryptography==50.0.2
olefile==0.47
# What ace3's xlmdeobfuscator module asks of its own rule file, python/ace4_python/xlmdeobfuscator.yar.
# ace3 has yara-python, which has no wheel for this Python and this image has no compiler; this is the
# engine ace-yara runs, at Cargo.lock's version. That goes beyond 4.1's rule.
yara-x==1.22.1

# ace3/Dockerfile installs these from each repository's master archive. These are the commits
# master was at on 2026-11-06, where master has been since 2021 and 2022: tag v1.3.4; version 0.0.9,
# which has no tag; and tag v0.2.7. Their files are the same as those in ace3's virtualenv.
xlrd2 @ https://github.com/DissectMalware/xlrd2/archive/74cd5302f9007f6cf9389f8819cf1676a1e2a717.zip
pyxlsb2 @ https://github.com/DissectMalware/pyxlsb2/archive/0a1ff1be329aa282ecbc347ff44fc6c07351685b.zip
XLMMacroDeobfuscator @ https://github.com/DissectMalware/XLMMacroDeobfuscator/archive/43114164d89b8b3b426144f1fdfeb2ca75d28b92.zip

